*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.profile text eol=lf

# Everything under engine-build is read inside a Linux container. pins.env is sourced by the build
# script, and with CRLF the shell tries to run the trailing carriage return as a command:
# `pins.env: line 7: $'\r': command not found`. Without this a Windows checkout produces an image
# that cannot run its own build, while CI — which checks out LF — passes.
engine-build/** text eol=lf

# ...except the built engine, which is committed and is BINARY. The rule above would rewrite CRLF
# inside a gzip stream and inside a WOFF2 font, which does not fail loudly — it produces an archive
# that will not inflate and a font that will not parse, on Windows only.
engine-build/out/** binary
